# Database and Prisma Rules

Database uses PostgreSQL + PostGIS.

Rules:
- Do not change schema unless task explicitly requests it.
- Use docs/database/schema-overview.md, docs/database/tables-catalog.md, and docs/database/enums.md as the current schema docs.
- No delivery_requests table.
- No impact_logs table.
- No impact_summaries table.
- No delivery_partners table.
- No partner_driver_profiles table.
- No MENTOR role.
- users table must not contain role column.
- user_roles supports multiple roles per user.
- Add UNIQUE(user_id, role) for user_roles.
- role_invitations stores token hash only.
- locations should support PostGIS geography(Point).
- reservations contains delivery fields.

When AI behavior, credit rules, logs, or matching logic changes:
- Update docs/features/ai-agent.md
- Update docs/flows/ai-material-matching-flow.md
- Update docs/database/tables-catalog.md if AI tables/fields changed

When schema, enums, relations, or migrations change:
- Update docs/database/schema-overview.md
- Update docs/database/tables-catalog.md
- Update docs/database/enums.md
- Update docs/08-implementation-status.md if capability status changed
- If unsure whether docs are needed, ask explicitly
